# Better Call Alex — environment variables (copy to .env; .env is gitignored)
#
# All of these are OPTIONAL: the app runs with defaults on a machine where
# the corpus was built into data/ and Ollama listens on the loopback default.

# Ollama daemon host. The daemon must be started with OLLAMA_NUM_CTX >= 32000
# and OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0 in ITS environment (see app/lib/llm.ts).
#OLLAMA_HOST=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# Repo root when running from outside the project directory. Auto-detected
# by walking up from CWD to the directory containing data/ otherwise.
#ALEX_REPO=/path/to/Better Call Alex

# Python interpreter for the eyecite verifier bridge. Defaults to
# .venv/bin/python when it exists, else `python3` on PATH.
#VERIFY_PYTHON=.venv/bin/python

# Force the synchronous verifier (spawnSync) even inside the server.
# Default: async bridge (spawn) when an event loop is present, sync for CLI.
#ALEX_VERIFY_SYNC=1

# =====================================================================
# ADR-004 — hybrid inference (Phase A). ALL OPTIONAL: without a key the
# app is local-only exactly as before.
# =====================================================================

# Per-run engine mode default: local | cloud | auto.
#   local  — everything on this machine (the original behavior).
#   cloud  — every stage on the OpenAI-compatible endpoint below.
#   auto   — per-stage routing via ALEX_AUTO_ROUTE (analyst+adversary ride
#            the frontier; intake+researcher stay local — the researcher
#            writes queries for OUR FTS dialect, where frontier models
#            can retrieve WORSE).
# The UI composer can override this per run. The verifier gates every
# engine identically (§5.1–5.2 are engine-agnostic by construction).
#
# With a key configured, "auto" is the intended default: reasoning-heavy
# stages (analyst, adversary) ride the cloud model; intake and the
# researcher stay local (the researcher writes queries for OUR FTS
# dialect, where frontier models can retrieve WORSE). "local" is the
# privacy/air-gapped default when no key is present.
#ALEX_ENGINE=auto

# OpenAI-compatible endpoint + key. NEVER commit the real key: .env is
# gitignored, and a guard test fails the build if the key name appears
# anywhere else. Rotate keys that have been shared in chat.
#ALEX_CLOUD_API_KEY=
#ALEX_CLOUD_MODEL=gpt-5
#
# Prefer provider aliases over numeric ids — numeric generations rot fast:
# (observed 2026-09-22 on Gemini's OpenAI-compat endpoint) gemini-2.0-flash
# served the canary, 404'd a full run minutes later ("no longer available",
# remediation pointed at a newer id); the /models list is stale too — it
# omits ids its chat endpoint serves (gemini-3.6-flash) and lists retired
# ones. gemini-flash-latest / gemini-flash-lite-latest track the current
# generation. The startup check WARNS only (lists lie; the first chat call
# is the authoritative loud failure).
#ALEX_CLOUD_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Cloud failure policy: abort (default — the run fails honestly) or local
# (fall back to the local tier WITH a disclosure audit row + UI badge).
#ALEX_CLOUD_FALLBACK=abort
# Per-call ceiling in ms.
#ALEX_CLOUD_TIMEOUT_MS=120000

# Auto-mode per-stage routing: stage:engine pairs, comma-separated.
# Stages: intake, researcher, analyst, adversary. Engines: local, cloud.
#ALEX_AUTO_ROUTE=analyst:cloud,adversary:cloud,intake:local,researcher:local
